  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Circular Economy in the Mekong Subregion: Needs, Challenges and Policy Recommendations for Viet Nam</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Mekong Subregion, comprising Myanmar, Laos, Thailand, Cambodia, and Viet Nam, is facing severe environmental degradation due to rapid urbanisation, population growth, and industrialisation. While sustainability efforts are underway, the transition to circular economy models remains uneven and constrained by significant policy, institutional, and behavioural barriers. This research seeks to address that gap by identifying practical needs, challenges, and opportunities for Viet Nam to promote circular economy in the broader Mekong Subregion. The findings will inform Vietnam&#x2019;s national policy development and foster regional partnerships for a more sustainable and resilient economic future. The study will support the UK&#x2019;s strategic priorities in the Mekong Subregion and in Vietnam, particularly in enhancing regional resilience, and fostering cooperation among sub-Mekong countries.</narrative>
  </description>
